-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/8c5aac28-c6d1-544c-98ab-0b80c6084ff5
-- title:
--   Uniqueness of an Igusa-component valuation subring over a supersingular place
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q \ge 5$, $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $A$ a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. $q$ is a nonunit of $A$. Two function fields occur: $\mathcal F_{M'} =$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (adjunction of the coefficientwise images) of the full level-$M'$ modular function field inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$, and $\mathcal F =$ `fieldBar q M'`, the corresponding base change of the $X_H$-function field of level $q^2M'$ for the subgroup `levelH q M'` (the kernel of the unit-group reduction map attached to the divisibility `dvd_sq_mul q M'`); the hypothesis `hle` asserts $\mathcal F_{M'} \subseteq \mathcal F$. On the characteristic-$q$ side, `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` is the intermediate field of $\mathrm{ResidueField}(A)((q))$ generated by $j$ and its $M'$-fold $q$-expansion. The finite set $W$ of places of this field over $\mathrm{ResidueField}(A)$ is required by `hW` to consist exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, that is of the places $w$ that are rational, satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value `w.evalAt (jGeomGen ...)` lies in `ssJSet q (ResidueField A)`.
--
--   The reduction datum is a `ConstantReduction` $R_0$ of $A$ from $\mathcal F_{M'}$ to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of $\mathcal F_{M'}$, a surjective residue homomorphism `R₀.residue` onto the characteristic-$q$ field with kernel the maximal ideal, a map `R₀.placeMap` on places, compatibility of the integers and of the residue with the constants $A$, the scaling property that every nonzero element becomes integral with nonzero residue after multiplication by a suitable constant, preservation of residue degrees of places, and compatibility of divisors with `Finsupp.mapDomain R₀.placeMap`. The hypothesis `hR₀` states that this reduction is computed coefficientwise: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ lies in $\mathcal F_{M'}$, that image lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue is, as a Laurent series over $\mathrm{ResidueField}(A)$, the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   Further arithmetic data: an element $\pi \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$ and $\pi \in A$, and an index $\zeta \in$ `Idx q`, i.e. a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. Two families of valuation subrings of $\mathcal F$ are given: $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$, indexed by $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q) =$ [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21), and $O_{\mathrm{ss}}$, indexed by $W$.
--
--   The hypotheses on the Igusa family are: `hIg_inf`, which describes $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ at the line `lineInfty q` as the set of $f \in \mathcal F$ for which there exist Laurent series $x, y$ over $A$ with the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ nonzero and $f \cdot y = x$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$; `hIg`, which provides for each line $\ell$ some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ whose reduction `redQ q γ` carries `lineInfty q` to $\ell$ and for which $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ is the preimage of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj`, the injectivity of $\ell \mapsto O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$; and `hIg_perm`, which asserts that for every index $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ taking preimages along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permutes the family, by a permutation $\sigma$ of $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q)$.
--
--   The hypotheses on the supersingular family are: `hSS_A`, that a constant $x \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$ if and only if $x \in A$; `hSS_over`, which says that for $s \in W$ and $f \in$ `R₀.integers` such that $f$ has nonnegative order at every place of $\mathcal F_{M'}$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which $\hat\jmath$ (the coefficientwise image of `jq`) has nonnegative order, and such that the $R_0$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ in $\mathcal F$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$, and moreover for every $a \in A$ whose residue in $\mathrm{ResidueField}(A)$ equals `s.evalAt` of the $R_0$-residue of $f$, the difference of the image of $f$ and the constant $a$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$ and in the maximal ideal of $O_{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$; `hSS_fix`, that each $O_{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$ is its own preimage under `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; and `hSS_tr`, that each $O_{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$ contains an element $t$ such that for every $a \in A$ the difference $t - a$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$ and is a unit there.
--
--   The descent data are: a subfield $K_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ algebraic over $K_0$ and $\pi \in K_0$; a henselian discrete valuation domain $A_0$ with an injective local homomorphism $\iota : A_0 \to A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is exactly $A \cap K_0$ (`hιK₀`), such that the composite of $\iota$ with the residue map of $A$ is surjective (`hres`), together with a generator $\varpi_0$ of the maximal ideal of $A_0$ (`hϖ₀`) satisfying $\iota(\varpi_0) = \pi$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (`hϖ₀π`); a subfield $F_0$ of $\mathcal F$ characterised by `hF₀` as the set of elements all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $K_0$; the hypothesis `hjF₀` that the image of $\hat\jmath$ in $\mathcal F$ lies in $F_0$, an $A_0$-algebra structure on $F_0$ whose structure map is, by `hj₀`, given by $\iota$ followed by the inclusion of constants $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to \mathcal F$, and the assumption that $\hat\jmath$ is nonzero as an element of $F_0$.
--
--   Finally, $s \in W$ and $\ell \in \mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q)$ are fixed, and $O_\ell :=$ `(OIg ℓ).comap F₀.subtype`, the descended Igusa valuation subring $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell) \cap F_0$ of $F_0$. Two valuation subrings $W_1, W_2$ of the residue field of $O_\ell$ are given, both distinct from $\top$ (`hW₁`, `hW₂`), subject to: the chart hypotheses `hC₁` and `hC₂`, that for every $g$ in the finite chart algebra `TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin A₀ ↥F₀ ĵ` — the subalgebra of elements of $F_0$ integral over the $A_0$-subalgebra generated by $\hat\jmath$ — which lies in $O_\ell$, the residue of $g$ belongs to $W_1$, respectively to $W_2$; and the reading hypotheses `hread₁` and `hread₂`, that for every $f \in$ `R₀.integers` satisfying the same two conditions as in `hSS_over` (nonnegative order wherever $\hat\jmath$ has nonnegative order, and $R_0$-residue in the valuation subring of $s$), for every $a \in A_0$ with the residue of $\iota(a)$ equal to `s.evalAt` of the $R_0$-residue of $f$, and for every $g$ in that chart algebra lying in $O_\ell$ whose image in $\mathcal F$ equals the image of $f$ minus the constant $\iota(a)$, the residue of $g$ in the residue field of $O_\ell$ lies in `W₁.nonunits`, respectively in `W₂.nonunits`.
--
--   The conclusion is the single equality $W_1 = W_2$.
--
--   Routine typeclass assumptions (primality, nonvanishing, decidability, the local algebra structures on the residue field of $A$) are present as instances.
--
--   This is the uniqueness half of the statement that on an Igusa component there is exactly one place above each supersingular place of the level-$M'$ floor, the total ramification of the Igusa curve over the supersingular points of Katz–Mazur, expressed in terms of valuation subrings of the residue field of a descended Igusa ring so that it applies to centres of closed points. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.eq_of_isMaximal_of_mem_nonunits_igusaRing_of_floorTrace_chartAlgFin_descent`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.eq_of_isMaximal_of_mem_nonunits_igusaRing_of_floorTrace_chartAlgFin_descent) and by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.eq_of_le_gaussRing_of_forall_isIntegral_mem_maximalIdeal_drinfeldRing_mem_nonunits_descent`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.eq_of_le_gaussRing_of_forall_isIntegral_mem_maximalIdeal_drinfeldRing_mem_nonunits_descent) in the construction of the semistable model of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_eq_of_valuationSubring_residueField_igusaRing_of_floorTrace_descent.lean

